# ovm settings: shipped by stack/obsidian. Every setting ovm reads.
#
# This machine's values go in ~/.config/ovm/ovm.local.env, beside this file (yours, never shipped).
# The environment wins over both: `OVM_PROBE_SECONDS=10 ovm list` does what it says. Format:
# NAME=value, one per line, read and never sourced (only a leading ~/, or a value that is ~, is
# expanded, to $HOME; a value may be quoted). A commented line is the default used when nothing
# sets it. `ovm config list` shows them and where each is from; `ovm config set NAME=value` writes
# ovm.local.env.

# Seconds ovm waits for a vault's ovm.yml to answer before it counts the vault unreachable (a vault
# on a hung iCloud or network mount blocks every read of it)
#OVM_PROBE_SECONDS=3
